--TEST--
A `Core` enum that moved into its class has no namespace name left: `Core\Order` names nothing, the error is reported where it is written, and it says where the enum went — `rule:enums/an-enum-lives-in-the-class-that-uses-it`, `rule:core-api/a-moved-name-says-where-it-went`
--FILE--
<?nvs
array<int> $nums = [3, 1, 2];
echo Core\Arr::sort($nums, {order: Core\Order::Desc})[0], "\n";
--EXPECT--

--EXPECTF-ERROR--
error[E0303]: `Core\Order` is not declared
  --> case.nvs:3:36
%A
  = help: `Core\Order` moved to `Core\Arr::Order`. Write `Core\Arr::Order` here
%A
error: aborting due to 1 error
To read what a code means and how to fix it, run `nvs agent show <code>`.
